.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Real laser beams are never perfectly diffraction-limited fundamental Gaussian modes: multimode content, aberrations, and gain-medium imperfections all make them diverge faster than an ideal beam of the same waist. Anthony Siegman showed that essentially every real laser beam&#x27;s second-moment width still propagates by the same functional form as an ideal Gaussian beam,">

